# Context101 — deploy.sh environment file
#
# Copy this file to either:
#   · cdk/.deploy-env             (per-repo, gitignored)
#   · ~/.context101/deploy-env    (per-user, shared across worktrees)
#
# chmod 600 the destination — these are real secrets.

# REQUIRED — gates the App Runner MCP service. Whatever string you pick
# becomes the shared bearer token your MCP clients send.
CTX_TOKEN="context101-platea-2026-bearer"

# OPTIONAL — only if Amplify should watch a GitHub repo. Omit both to
# deploy the AWS stack without a GitHub-watched web app.
# REPOSITORY="https://github.com/<you>/context101"
# CTX_GH_TOKEN="ghp_..."

# OPTIONAL — Bedrock embedding model for the default brain.
# Skip / omit to keep amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0. Pick any Amazon
# Titan or Cohere embedding model enabled in Model access.
# EMBED_MODEL_ID="amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0"

# OPTIONAL — passed through to the cdk subprocess.
AWS_PROFILE="plateapr.com"

# OPTIONAL — OpenSaaS/Postgres + Better Auth path.
# Omit DATABASE_URL and set CREATE_RDS=true to let CDK provision
# a small public RDS Postgres (db.t3.micro). The password stays in
# Secrets Manager (ControlPlaneDbSecretArn) and is never printed.
# CREATE_RDS="true"
# DATABASE_URL should be your Postgres connection string.
# Neon URLs auto-select DATABASE_DRIVER=neon-http. Supabase/RDS/local Postgres
# can use DATABASE_DRIVER=postgres-js.
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://..."
# DATABASE_DRIVER="neon-http"
# DATABASE_PREPARE="true"
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET="$(openssl rand -base64 32)"
# Leave BETTER_AUTH_URL / APP_URL unset so CDK binds Better Auth to
# Amplify's default domain (https://main.<app-id>.amplifyapp.com).
# Set them only if you bring your own host. Never the hosted product.
# BETTER_AUTH_URL="https://kb.example.com"
# MCP_TOKEN_PEPPER="$(openssl rand -base64 32)"
#
# Deployment mode:
# self_hosted = first-run setup/admin invite flow, no public signup by default
# hosted      = public signup/onboarding/billing flow
# APP_MODE="self_hosted"
# ALLOW_PUBLIC_SIGNUP="false"
# BILLING_ENABLED="false"
# APP_URL="https://kb.example.com"
# MCP_PUBLIC_HOST="https://mcp.example.com"
#
# Transactional email (hosted paid default: AWS SES).
# SES_FROM_EMAIL must be a verified SES identity.
# SES_REGION="us-east-1"
# SES_FROM_EMAIL="Context101 <no-reply@your-domain.com>"
# SES_REPLY_TO_EMAIL="support@your-domain.com"
#
# Magic-link sign-in reuses SES_* + APP_URL / BETTER_AUTH_URL (no extra
# secrets). Optional Better Auth origin allow-list if a browser Origin is sent:
# BETTER_AUTH_TRUSTED_ORIGINS="https://app.example.com"

# OPTIONAL — instance connector OAuth / GitHub App. These are Secrets Manager
# *names* (ids), not client_secret / PEM / PAT values. Create the provider
# app, then `context101 connectors` (TTY wizard) or
# `context101 connectors setup google|notion|github` writes the
# SM secret and these keys. CDK defaults (NAME_PREFIX=context101):
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET_ID="context101-google-oauth-client"
# NOTION_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET_ID="context101-notion-oauth-client"
# GitHub App lives at <NAME_PREFIX>-connector-github-app (PAT is per-connector
# in admin, not here).
# GITHUB_APP_SECRET_ID="context101-connector-github-app"
# After setup: `context101 update`, then Add source → Connect in admin.
#
# OPTIONAL — Google Drive picker in Add source (Docs / Sheets / Slides).
# Browser API key + Cloud project *number* (not the project id string).
# Never commit real keys. Enable Picker API + Drive API on the same
# project as the OAuth web client (`context101-connectors` on hosted).
# Add the admin origin as an Authorized JavaScript origin on that client.
# Consent: first Connect asks for drive.file + Docs/Sheets/Slides readonly.
# Alternative: `context101 connectors setup google` prompts for
# picker_api_key / picker_app_id (or --picker-api-key / --picker-app-id)
# and merges them onto the OAuth SM secret. Omit / empty keeps existing.
# --clear-picker drops those fields. Never commit real keys.
# GOOGLE_PICKER_API_KEY=""
# GOOGLE_PICKER_APP_ID=""
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_PICKER_API_KEY and NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_PICKER_APP_ID
# also work (inlined at Next build). Prefer the server names above.
